/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same engine has a centre crankshaft with the crankpin centre 100 mm from each main bearing centre. With the crank at top dead centre and the gas force of 31 416 N on the crankpin, check the 56 mm crankpin in bending for an allowable stress of 75 MPa, and resize it if needed. Ignore the flywheel.
   1. Reactions: by symmetry R1 = R2 = 31 416/2 = 15 708 N.
   2. Bending moment at the crankpin centre: M = R1 × 100 = 1 570 800 N·mm.
   3. Stress at dc = 56 mm: σb = 32M/(πdc³) = 32 × 1 570 800/(π × 56³) = 91.1 MPa, above 75 MPa.
   4. Resize: dc³ = 32M/(π × 75) = 213 330 mm³, dc = 59.8 mm. Adopt 60 mm.
   5. Check at 60 mm: σb = 74.1 MPa ≤ 75 MPa; bearing pressure with lc = 60 mm: 31 416/(60 × 60) = 8.73 MPa ≤ 10 MPa.
   Answer: The 56 mm crankpin chosen for bearing pressure fails in bending (91.1 MPa); a 60 mm × 60 mm crankpin passes both checks. */
