/* book exam traps: Designing the rod for crushing (σc A) alone. It is a column, so Rankine’s formula with the slenderness L/kxx sets the size. | Using kyy and length L together. Buckling about yy has equivalent length L/2; the I-section is designed about xx with length L. | Forgetting the factor of safety on the gas force before entering Rankine’s formula. | Sizing the crankpin by bearing pressure and stopping. At top dead centre it must also pass the bending check, as the second example shows. | Checking the crankshaft only at top dead centre. The maximum-torque position adds torsion and can govern the shaft next to the web. */
